{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898007-faerie-based-bloodlines","id":898007,"title":"Faerie based bloodlines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T11:05:48-07:00","id":898007,"title":"Faerie based bloodlines?","content":"I wonder if anyone has created or there exists any bloodlines that are Faerie based that especially works best for a Requiem and Lost crossover?<br /> <br /> Especially the bloodlines align with their respective clans and seemings?<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Darkling = Mehket<br /> <br /> Fairest = Daeva or Ventrue<br /> <br /> Beast = Gangrel<br /> <br /> Ogre = Nosferatu<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the Elemental and Wizened would fit under though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-24-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:27:51-07:00","id":898018,"title":"","content":"Bloodline? I don't recall. However there is a Covenant in Dance Macabre that does pretty well kinda, Children of Thorns, pg. 92","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:30:00-07:00","id":898022,"title":"","content":"I would recommend looking at the conversions done to bring the Ravnos Clan from Masquerade into line with Requiem rules for a Fae touched take on Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:26:45-07:00","id":899573,"title":"","content":"As long as the K-word isn't brought up, I'm good. *glowers at the blue-skinned bastards* I do like the Children of Thorns from DM, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:42:00-07:00","id":900224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898007-faerie-based-bloodlines?p=899573#post899573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the K-word isn't brought up, I'm good. *glowers at the blue-skinned bastards* I do like the Children of Thorns from DM, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiasyd Kiasyd Kiasyd<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a more serious, helpful sort of note, I wrote up a 1e bloodline a long while back (I'll have to see if I saved it anywhere) for Nosferatu that was basically along the lines of embracing the monstrous oddities of the hedge and the fae as a potential 'home' for outcast kindred like themselves. They gained a &quot;discipline&quot; that let them learn a number of 'fae tricks', which were all of fairly low power (though with decent utility), but raising the discipline let you choose an increasingly higher number of them each time (1, 3, 6, 10, 15 I think). A rare few of the tricks ate up more than one of those slots.<br /> <br /> Some of these 'tricks' included gaining a 'mask' to veil the Nosferatu weakness (for a time, and with a cost, and with no effect on those that could see past fae masks either), learning to subsist on glamour to a limited extent, and a few that basically mirrored low level contracts, among other things. <br /> <br /> Whether or not I have the writeup still, might be fun to try rewriting them for 2e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T10:20:14-07:00","id":902126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898007-faerie-based-bloodlines?p=900224#post900224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kiasyd Kiasyd Kiasyd</div> </div> </div> </div>*eye twitch*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/898007-faerie-based-bloodlines?p=900224#post900224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious, helpful sort of note, I wrote up a 1e bloodline a long while back (I'll have to see if I saved it anywhere) for Nosferatu that was basically along the lines of embracing the monstrous oddities of the hedge and the fae as a potential 'home' for outcast kindred like themselves. They gained a &quot;discipline&quot; that let them learn a number of 'fae tricks', which were all of fairly low power (though with decent utility), but raising the discipline let you choose an increasingly higher number of them each time (1, 3, 6, 10, 15 I think). A rare few of the tricks ate up more than one of those slots.<br /> <br /> Some of these 'tricks' included gaining a 'mask' to veil the Nosferatu weakness (for a time, and with a cost, and with no effect on those that could see past fae masks either), learning to subsist on glamour to a limited extent, and a few that basically mirrored low level contracts, among other things.<br /> <br /> Whether or not I have the writeup still, might be fun to try rewriting them for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound pretty cool, actually. Wouldn't mind seeing a 2e version of that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}